WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
What if your factory needs 20% more output?
Do you need more equipment?

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.500
Rebalance machining operations across the same four cells and 48 CNCs.

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:22.000
Modeled annual capacity rises from 115,200 to 132,822 units — up 15.3%.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Automated process planning

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Inspect the part, cutter, original NC and toolpath in detail.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Verify the completed geometry before production handover.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Automated fixture design and BOM generation

8
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Inspect bore clamps on both faces and the work supports.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Rotate the completed fixture to review every side.

10
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Tool quantities and tooling costs update with the production plan.

11
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.000
From the completed P06 fixture to the new workplace.
Production and logistics continue.

12
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Track each pallet’s LOT, completed quantity and transport plan.

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:38.967
Zoom into Workplace 4 and continue on the same simulation clock.

14
00:01:38.967 --> 00:01:41.967
SCADA + cell simulation · 2× playback

15
00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:49.467
Unload P01 and transfer the part to P02.

16
00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:57.217
Collect new stock and return along the LM axis.

17
00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:05.467
Load P01, secure the fixture, then retract the gripper.

18
00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.967
Close the door and resume machining.

19
00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:15.967
Review and approve a bore-position change.
Verify the revised geometry and NC together.

20
00:02:15.967 --> 00:02:21.467
Compare a sample measurement with the design.
Review the proposed NC correction.

21
00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:30.467
Optimize factory routes, dispatch and cell handling.
Modeled annual capacity reaches 138,596 units — up 20.3%.

22
00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:35.467
Making every factory flow like water. This is Flowmatic.
